---
description: Prefer CSS custom properties and design tokens in Frontend SCSS
globs: App/**/*.{scss,css,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# CSS variables first

When writing or editing Frontend styles/components, prefer CSS custom properties (design tokens and component vars) over raw lengths, `%` fills, or one-off calcs.

## Do

- Size icons/spinners/chrome with tokens: `var(--kicl-size-*)`, gutters `var(--kicl-gutter-*)`, durations `var(--kicl-transition-duration-*)`.
- Position in JSX: `kicl-position-*` utility classes (see design-system rule) — do not set `position` in SCSS.
- Component SCSS: define defaults on `:root` as `--kicl--components--{name}--*`, apply via `var(...)`, override those vars in modifiers — not duplicate property blocks with magic numbers.
- Colors/fills/type in JSX: prefer `kicl-*` utility classes (see design-system rule); in SCSS backgrounds/borders still use `var(--kicl-color-*)`.

```scss
// ✅ Spinner icon — token, not parent %
--kicl--components--spinner--svg--block-size: var(--kicl-size-2x);
--kicl--components--spinner--svg--inline-size: var(--kicl-size-2x);

// ✅ Modifier overrides the variable
&--position--overlay {
  --kicl--components--spinner--block-size: 100%;
  --kicl--components--spinner--inline-size: 100%;
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ Position via utility class
<div className="kicl-position-absolute" />
```

## Don't

```scss
// ❌ Icon fills the overlay container
--kicl--components--spinner--svg--block-size: 100%;
--kicl--components--spinner--svg--inline-size: 100%;

// ❌ Position in SCSS (use `kicl-position-*` in JSX)
position: absolute;
position: var(--kicl-position-absolute);

// ❌ Invented scales
width: calc(var(--kicl-gutter) * 1.7);
font-size: 14px;
```

## Spinner specifically

- Overlay may be `100%` for the **backdrop** box only.
- The **icon** stays a fixed token (`--kicl-size-2x` by default); size variants should adjust component vars / scale, not stretch to the parent.
- Page/route loading fallbacks: prefer `position="inline"` when a full-bleed overlay isn’t intended.
